## Building a Password Generator

### Character Sets

```xiom
fn get_lowers() -> Str { "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz" }
fn get_uppers() -> Str { "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ" }
fn get_digits() -> Str { "0123456789" }
fn get_symbols() -> Str { "!@#$%^&*()-_=+" }
```

### Building the Character Pool

```xiom
fn build_pool(use_upper: Bool, use_digits: Bool, use_symbols: Bool) -> Str {
  let mut pool = get_lowers();
  if use_upper { pool = string.str_concat(pool, get_uppers()); };
  if use_digits { pool = string.str_concat(pool, get_digits()); };
  if use_symbols { pool = string.str_concat(pool, get_symbols()); };
  pool
}
```

### Generating the Password

```xiom
fn generate_password(length: Int, pool: Str, seed: Int) -> Str {
  let mut password = "";
  let mut state = seed;
  let mut i = 0;
  while i < length {
    state = (state * 1103515245 + 12345) % 2147483648;
    let idx = state % pool.len();
    password = string.str_concat(password, string.from_char(pool.get(idx).unwrap()));
    i += 1;
  };
  password
}
```

### Validating Password Strength

```xiom
fn has_upper(s: Str) -> Bool { /* check for A-Z */ }
fn has_digit(s: Str) -> Bool { /* check for 0-9 */ }
fn has_symbol(s: Str) -> Bool { /* check for special chars */ }

fn is_strong_password(s: Str) -> Bool {
  s.len() >= 8 && has_upper(s) && has_digit(s) && has_symbol(s)
}
```

